description:
FILED s534 (reviewing session, Opus 5.5, 2026-11-06) from the PPI-under-PCL profile the USER asked for (docs/eval-in-cl-plan.md §4.6 "MEASURED s534").  PRE-EXISTING on main 59317afd.

MECHANISM (read, cl/pcl-runtime.lisp box-set general path ~4374): `(unless (zerop (hash-table-count *p-weak-boxes*)) (remhash box *p-weak-boxes*))` -- the pos()-table trick (#2539): skip the remhash while the table is empty.  But the table is WEAK (`:weakness :key`), and EVERY SBCL weak-table operation (gethash / puthash / remhash) runs under `sb-thread::call-with-recursive-system-lock` + without-interrupts.  Once a program has called `Scalar::Util::weaken` ONCE (PPI weakens every parent link; Moo, Mojo, Template-Toolkit and cache-keeping modules do too), the table is non-empty for the rest of the run and every general-path store (a reference, an object, a non-simple string ...) pays a locked remhash.

MEASURED: sb-sprof of PPI parsing lib/Math/BigInt/Calc.pm 20x under PCL (28,943 samples, quiet box): box-set 10.5 % total, of which remhash -> remhash/weak -> call-with-recursive-system-lock = 8.7 % of the WHOLE run (~11.5 % of the parse loop).  Plus gethash/weak 4.7 % (object-address = refaddr, %pcl-isa-ancestry, %p-isa-parent-names, find-in-class) -- each a locked weak lookup too.

REPRODUCER (the cost appears only after a weaken; perl has none):
    use Scalar::Util qw(weaken); use Time::HiRes qw(time);
    if ($ENV{WEAKEN}) { my $r = []; my $x = $r; weaken($x) }
    my @o = map { [$_] } 1 .. 10; my $t = time; my $s;
    for my $i (1 .. 1_000_000) { $s = $o[$i % 10] }
    printf "%.3f s\n", time - $t;
  PCL (load 26 -- noisy, re-measure quiet): WEAKEN=0 0.063-0.136 s, WEAKEN=1 0.275-0.388 s (2-6x); perl 0.10-0.14 s either way.

FIX SHAPE (measure first; sign-off rule): make the per-store question NOT touch the weak table -- e.g. a bit on the box itself ("this box was handed to weaken"), set by weaken, tested by box-set (a slot read), cleared with the table entry; the table stays for isweak's answer, or the bit IS the answer and the table goes.  Check p-box's slot layout first (a new slot is a word per box: measure RSS on the everyday battery).  For the gethash/weak half: object-address (refaddr) and the isa caches -- ask whether they need WEAK tables or can key on something that lives in the object.  Bars: the reproducer WEAKEN=1 == WEAKEN=0 within noise; tools/bench-exec.pl unchanged; the PPI-under-PCL parse time (docs/eval-in-cl-plan.md §4.6's bench) BEFORE -> AFTER; gate + sweep (a cl/ change).  Related: #582 (the per-class method cache -- the other, larger half of PPI's 3.8x), #2191 / #2421 (eval compile cost), #4480 (eval in CL).


=== s534a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08): where the weak-table locks OVERLAP method dispatch (noted, not fixed here) ===

`%p-isa-symbol` (every @ISA reader: p-method-call's prologue and walk, %p-isa-parent-names, %pcl-find-method-in-chain, %pcl-find-autoload-in-isa, %pcl-isa-ancestry) calls `(gethash sym *p-stash-deleted*)` with NO count guard on a `:weakness :key` table: 19.1 % of the methinh3 bench row, 11.2 % methinh, 11.4 % methpoly, 18.2 % ovlbool (sb-sprof, base 95a1de03).  The one-line count guard is filed as #4525 (measured: -16..-31 % on those rows, -10 % on the PPI parse).  The table's keys are INTERNED symbols (their package keeps them alive), so it need not be weak at all -- that removes the lock even in a program that has deleted a stash entry; decide it here with box-set's remhash.  docs/method-lookup-eval-s534.md §2.
